! Class !! Mechanism (hypothesized) !! Detectable signature
|-
| '''Photic-band entrainment''' || 3–8 Hz pulsed RF or visible-light flicker at high amplitude, exploiting the known photic-driving response in EEG. || ELF modulation envelope detectable by an SDR or RF envelope detector; visible flicker by a fast photodiode.
|-
| '''Cardiac-rate modulation''' || Modulation of an RF carrier at 0.8–2 Hz, hypothesised to couple to vagal tone and HRV. || Slow modulation envelope; correlated dip in operator HRV.
|-
| '''Sustained demoralisation field''' || Low-amplitude wideband RF or ELF persisting for minutes-to-hours, hypothesised to suppress operator coherence. || Elevated wideband noise floor; persistent operator HRV / EEG-alpha depression.
|-
